abstract: >
  VeriSigil Constitutional Charter v1.0 defines the formal standard for verifiable,
  cryptographically provable AI execution governance. It specifies the Constitutional
  Cognitive Infrastructure (CCI) model comprising four constitutional layers (A: Cognitive
  Formation, B: Constitutional Runtime, C: Cryptographic Sovereignty, D: Sovereign Governance
  Mesh), eight constitutional invariants (VGS-ELI-INV-001 through VGS-ELI-INV-008), the
  ten-stage VeriSigil Constitutional Execution Model (VCEM), VeriLanguage (VSL) grammar
  specification, and the VeriVM governance runtime architecture. This charter establishes
  the reference standard for systems claiming constitutional admissibility of autonomous
  AI execution.

